00:12:52.760 --> 00:12:53.620
Rainn, what are you doing?
雷恩，你在干什么？

348
00:12:53.700 --> 00:12:54.620
Why are you calling us?
你为什么要给我们打电话？

349
00:12:54.880 --> 00:12:56.880
Well, I just wanted to see how you guys are doing.
噢，我只是想看看你们过得怎么样。

350
00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:57.820
I missed you.
我想你们了。

351
00:12:57.940 --> 00:12:58.700
I missed you.
我想你了。

352
00:12:59.840 --> 00:13:01.460
I just want to know if you want to hang out.
我只是想知道你想不想出来聚聚。

353
00:13:01.980 --> 00:13:03.380
Oh, I do want to hang out.
噢，我当然想聚聚。

354
00:13:03.380 --> 00:13:04.400
I would like to hang out.
我很想聚聚。

355
00:13:04.940 --> 00:13:05.340
Great.
太好了。

356
00:13:05.740 --> 00:13:07.080
So when are we getting together?
那我们什么时候见面？

357
00:13:07.540 --> 00:13:08.540
You tell us.
你们定吧。

358
00:13:08.680 --> 00:13:10.840
You know what we want to do, Rainn, for reals.
雷恩，说真的，你知道我们想做什么。

359
00:13:10.940 --> 00:13:12.420
We had this on the text thread.
我们在群聊里提过这事。

360
00:13:12.760 --> 00:13:17.620
We want to come to your house and listen to Creed and your son play guitar together.
我们想去你家，听克里德和你儿子一起弹吉他。

361
00:13:17.860 --> 00:13:21.460
And I want to see your new place, and I want to meet your pigs and your zonkey.
我还想看看你的新家，想见见你的猪和斑驴。

362
00:13:21.740 --> 00:13:24.020
Have you heard about our newest pet sensation?
你们听说我们家新来的宠物明星了吗？

363
00:13:24.700 --> 00:13:25.080
No.
没有。

364
00:13:25.080 --> 00:13:26.160
Oh, the peacock!
噢，是孔雀！

365
00:13:26.340 --> 00:13:28.080
We have Alma the peacock.
我们养了一只叫阿尔玛的孔雀。

366
00:13:28.600 --> 00:13:33.040
And now, Rainn, did she just walk on up, or how did Alma get there?
雷恩，它是自己走过来的，还是怎么到你那儿的？

367
00:13:33.480 --> 00:13:37.280
So my wife had a horse for a long time named Gus.
我妻子养了一匹马很久了，叫格斯。

368
00:13:37.840 --> 00:13:42.800
And Gus was a very old, white, Lipizzan horse, and he passed away this summer.
格斯是一匹年纪很大的白色利比扎马，它今年夏天去世了。

369
00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:47.860
He lived a rich, full horse life, and he died very quickly.
它度过了充实而圆满的一生，走得很快。

370
00:13:47.940 --> 00:13:49.500
So that was all fine.
所以一切都还好。

371
00:13:49.800 --> 00:13:58.080
But his stall was empty, and they put a vase of flowers in there, and it was just kind of left empty as a kind of a salute to old Gus.
但它的马厩空了下来，他们在里面放了一瓶花，算是对老格斯的纪念，就那样空着。

372
00:13:58.080 --> 00:14:03.080
And two weeks later, no joke, and Gus was white, by the way.
两周后，真的不骗你，顺便说一下，格斯是白色的。

373
00:14:03.600 --> 00:14:12.660
Two weeks later, out of nowhere, sitting in Gus's horse stall was a white peahen, a female peacock.
两周后，不知从哪儿冒出来一只白色雌孔雀，坐在了格斯的马厩里。

374
00:14:12.880 --> 00:14:13.900
Oh, my goodness.
天哪。

375
00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:14.780
Whoa.
哇。

376
00:14:14.780 --> 00:14:16.440
No one knows where it came from.
没人知道它是从哪儿来的。

377
00:14:16.440 --> 00:14:18.300
It had never been seen there previously.
以前从来没见过它。

378
00:14:18.560 --> 00:14:24.100
It hadn't been seen in the neighborhood or the area of where my wife's horse, where she rides her horses.
在附近或者我妻子骑马的地方也从没见过它。

379
00:14:24.100 --> 00:14:26.720
And it just moved in to his stall.
它就那样搬进了格斯的马厩。

380
00:14:27.140 --> 00:14:36.960
And so she kind of trained it to eat feed, and it couldn't stay there because it was spooking some of the horses because it would flap around and squawk.
我妻子训练它吃饲料，但它不能一直待在那儿，因为它会扑腾和尖叫，吓到了其他马。

381
00:14:37.460 --> 00:14:49.800
And so she trained it to eat feed and go into a carrying container bin, and we took it to our house, and it made the transition perfectly.
于是她训练它吃饲料并走进运输箱，我们把它带回了家，它适应得非常完美。

382
00:14:49.800 --> 00:14:56.780
And you guys, Alma is amazing, and she sleeps during the day when she's not hunting bugs.
伙计们，阿尔玛太神奇了，它白天不抓虫子的时候就在睡觉。

383
00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:01.640
She sleeps in the olive tree right outside my office window and just stares in at me all day.
它睡在我办公室窗外的橄榄树上，整天盯着我看。

384
00:15:01.780 --> 00:15:08.220
So if I'm, like, podcasting or on Zoom calls or whatever, I have a white peacock staring into my office.
所以如果我在录播客或者开视频会议什么的，就会有一只白孔雀盯着我的办公室。

385
00:15:08.640 --> 00:15:10.640
This is all I could ever hope for, Rain.
雷恩，这简直是我梦寐以求的。

386
00:15:10.660 --> 00:15:12.460
I'm excited about my hummingbirds.
我还在为我的蜂鸟感到兴奋呢。

387
00:15:12.460 --> 00:15:14.940
If I had a peacock in my tree, I'd lose it.
如果我树上有一只孔雀，我肯定会疯掉的。

388
00:15:15.220 --> 00:15:17.260
I mean, Rain, it's Gus.
我是说，雷恩，那就是格斯。

389
00:15:17.260 --> 00:15:17.880
That's so cool.
太酷了。

390
00:15:18.020 --> 00:15:18.960
It's Gus, right?
那是格斯，对吧？

391
00:15:18.960 --> 00:15:23.980
My friend said if there was ever more proof needed for reincarnation.
我朋友说，如果还需要更多关于轮回的证据的话。

392
00:15:24.160 --> 00:15:29.200
Now, I don't know that I buy reincarnation, but, I mean, it was magical.
我不知道我是否相信轮回，但我是说，这太神奇了。

393
00:15:29.420 --> 00:15:31.280
It's a magical experience.
这是一种神奇的体验。

394
00:15:31.940 --> 00:15:33.300
It's kind of crazy.
这简直太疯狂了。

395
00:15:33.540 --> 00:15:35.080
Well, there's something happening there.
嗯，这其中肯定有什么玄机。

396
00:15:35.100 --> 00:15:40.980
Yeah, I was going to say, whether you believe in reincarnation or not, there's just something beautiful in the universe that happened right there.
是啊，我正想说，不管你信不信轮回，宇宙中确实发生了一些美妙的事情。

397
00:15:41.120 --> 00:15:41.660
That's right.
没错。

398
00:15:41.960 --> 00:15:42.100
Yeah.
是啊。

399
00:15:42.340 --> 00:15:47.300
So besides now our pigs that live at our house, now we have a peacock who is very demanding.
所以除了现在住在我们家的猪，我们还有了一只非常挑剔的孔雀。

400
00:15:47.300 --> 00:15:49.220
Holly, my wife, just went crazy.
我妻子霍莉简直要疯了。

401
00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:52.380
She bought, like, a big box arrived yesterday.
她买的东西，昨天到了一个大箱子。

402
00:15:52.380 --> 00:15:57.380
And I opened it up and it was filled, I'm not kidding you, it was filled with mealworMs.
我把它打开一看，里面装满了，我没开玩笑，全是面包虫。

403
00:15:57.400 --> 00:15:57.740
Ew.
呃。

404
00:15:59.840 --> 00:16:04.880
Two, like, 20 pound boxes of bags of mealworMs.
两箱，大概每箱20磅的面包虫。

405
00:16:04.920 --> 00:16:05.960
Where do you keep those?
你把那些东西放哪儿？

406
00:16:06.100 --> 00:16:06.300
Yeah.
是啊。

407
00:16:06.520 --> 00:16:07.540
Do you refrigerate them?
你需要冷藏它们吗？

408
00:16:07.540 --> 00:16:08.100
God save us.
天哪，救救我们吧。

409
00:16:08.100 --> 00:16:09.500
Like, what do you do with the meal?
就是，你拿这些虫子怎么办？

410
00:16:09.680 --> 00:16:10.920
Where do you put a mealworm?
你把面包虫放在哪儿？

411
00:16:11.640 --> 00:16:15.200
You just put them on the ground and then she eats the mealworMs.
你就把它们撒在地上，然后她就会吃掉那些面包虫。

412
00:16:15.320 --> 00:16:16.700
But in between eating.
但在吃东西的间隙呢？

413
00:16:16.920 --> 00:16:18.400
Not my wife, the peacock.
不是我老婆，是那只孔雀。

414
00:16:18.480 --> 00:16:18.960
The peacock.
那只孔雀。

415
00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:19.960
We got that part.
我们明白这一点。

416
00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.980
Well, Rain, listen, we're so excited to have you on.
好吧，雷恩，听着，我们很高兴你能来。

417
00:16:23.080 --> 00:16:26.740
We know you've been on before and you've sent in audio clips and you're always so supportive.
我们知道你之前来过，也发过音频片段，你一直都很支持我们。

418
00:16:27.240 --> 00:16:34.640
But we realize there are just some real general questions we ask our guests and we never got to do that with you.
但我们意识到，有些我们通常会问嘉宾的问题，我们还没来得及问你。

419
00:16:34.900 --> 00:16:37.480
And here is the one we always lead with.
这是我们总是会先问的一个问题。

420
00:16:37.580 --> 00:16:38.060
Are you ready?
准备好了吗？

421
00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:39.740
Okay, hit me.
好的，尽管问吧。

422
00:16:40.140 --> 00:16:40.580
All right.
好的。

423
00:16:40.980 --> 00:16:44.240
So how did you get your job on The Office?
那么你是怎么得到《办公室》里那个角色的？

424
00:16:44.280 --> 00:16:47.540
Is it true that you first auditioned for the role of Michael Scott?
传闻你最初试镜的角色是迈克尔·斯科特，这是真的吗？

425
00:16:47.760 --> 00:16:50.100
Tell us your Office origin story.
给我们讲讲你出演《办公室》的起源故事吧。

426
00:16:50.380 --> 00:16:52.640
Oh, I have a great Office origin story.
哦，我有一个很棒的《办公室》起源故事。

427
00:16:53.840 --> 00:16:55.360
I love to tell the story.
我特别喜欢讲这个故事。

428
00:16:55.420 --> 00:16:55.980
It's fantastic.
太精彩了。

429
00:16:56.300 --> 00:17:01.780
I was starting to do this show Six Feet Under and I was just at the very beginning of that show.
当时我刚开始拍《六英尺下》，正处于那部剧的起步阶段。

430
00:17:01.980 --> 00:17:04.880
And that was right when HBO was starting to take off.
那正好是HBO开始腾飞的时候。

431
00:17:04.880 --> 00:17:09.420
And it was a very widely, highly regarded show.
那是一部评价非常高、备受推崇的剧。

432
00:17:09.920 --> 00:17:16.240
And I got cast in this Janine Garofalo comedy pilot for ABC.
然后我被选中出演珍妮·加罗法洛为ABC制作的一部喜剧试播集。

433
00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:22.340
And, you know, it was a very small role, but I was like, hey, you know, it's an amazing paycheck.
你知道，那只是个很小的角色，但我当时想，嘿，这薪水可真不错。

434
00:17:23.000 --> 00:17:24.780
Um, this is great.
嗯，这太棒了。

435
00:17:24.940 --> 00:17:25.920
I'm going to be a series regular.
我要成为常驻演员了。

436
00:17:25.920 --> 00:17:29.920
It's my first, like, real stab at a series regular job.
这是我第一次真正尝试担任常驻演员的工作。

437
00:17:30.580 --> 00:17:33.580
And which is a lot better money than doing a guest star.
这比做客串演员的收入要好得多。

438
00:17:33.740 --> 00:17:33.860
Right.
没错。

439
00:17:33.860 --> 00:17:35.220
Just for those who are listening and wondering.
顺便告诉那些正在收听并感到好奇的听众。

440
00:17:35.500 --> 00:17:37.060
And I was very excited about it.
我当时对此感到非常兴奋。

441
00:17:37.600 --> 00:17:38.840
Bob Odenkirk was in it.
鲍勃·奥登科克也在里面。

442
00:17:39.120 --> 00:17:40.680
Mark Maron was in it.
马克·马龙也在里面。

443
00:17:40.840 --> 00:17:40.890
What?
什么？

444
00:17:40.890 --> 00:17:42.220
It had a really kind of great caSt.
那部剧的演员阵容真的很棒。

445
00:17:42.560 --> 00:17:44.800
And I was walking to the table read.
当时我正走去参加剧本围读会。

446
00:17:45.020 --> 00:17:46.060
Wait, wait, Rain, Rain.
等等，等等，雷恩，雷恩。

447
00:17:46.180 --> 00:17:46.880
What was it called?
那部剧叫什么名字？

448
00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:47.980
Do you know the name of it?
你知道它的名字吗？

449
00:17:52.920 --> 00:17:55.520
Real life, still life, something like that.
《真实生活》、《静物生活》，大概是这类名字。

450
00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:56.460
I'll look it up.
我会去查一下。

451
00:17:56.640 --> 00:17:56.860
Real life.
现实生活。

452
00:17:56.880 --> 00:17:57.700
Go on, go on, go on.
继续，继续，继续。

453
00:17:57.820 --> 00:17:58.400
I can't remember.
我不记得了。

454
00:18:00.120 --> 00:18:04.600
And I was on the way to the table read, which is something that actors you do at the studio
当时我正要去参加剧本围读，这是演员在制片厂常做的事，

455
00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:05.480
or you used to do.
或者说以前常做的事。

456
00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:08.780
You all sit in a room behind a table and you read it out loud.
大家坐在桌子后面，把剧本大声读出来。

457
00:18:08.980 --> 00:18:12.820
And all the executives are there so they can kind of see the cast together, get their
所有高管都会到场，这样他们能看到演员们聚在一起，感受他们的

458
00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:16.340
energy, hear the rhythms of the read, give notes, et cetera.
活力，听听台词的节奏，给出意见等等。

459
00:18:17.100 --> 00:18:18.280
Very common occurrence.
非常普遍的情况。

460
00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:29.480
But on my way there, I ran into this NBC executive that I knew at the time, who I had met a couple
但在去的路上，我碰到了当时认识的一位NBC高管，我之前见过他

461
00:18:29.480 --> 00:18:29.760
of times.
几次。

462
00:18:29.900 --> 00:18:30.920
I forget why.
我不记得为什么了。

463
00:18:31.340 --> 00:18:32.580
And I was like, oh, hi.
我就说，哦，嗨。

464
00:18:32.720 --> 00:18:34.000
It was Vernon, Vernon Sanders.
是弗农，弗农·桑德斯。

465
00:18:34.160 --> 00:18:35.340
Oh, we love Vernon.
哦，我们喜欢弗农。

466
00:18:35.740 --> 00:18:36.100
Yes.
是的。

467
00:18:36.380 --> 00:18:36.920
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

468
00:18:37.100 --> 00:18:38.200
He's in Amazon now.
他现在在亚马逊。

469
00:18:38.460 --> 00:18:39.580
And a nice guy.
人很好。

470
00:18:39.740 --> 00:18:40.820
And I was like, hi, Vernon.
我就说，嗨，弗农。

471
00:18:40.900 --> 00:18:41.520
And he's like, hi.
他说，嗨。

472
00:18:41.620 --> 00:18:42.780
He's like, what's going on?
他问，最近怎么样？

473
00:18:42.780 --> 00:18:48.600
And he goes, well, I'm so excited because we just landed the rights to the BBC office.
他说，我太兴奋了，因为我们刚拿下了BBC版《办公室》的版权。

474
00:18:49.780 --> 00:18:52.760
And I had seen a couple episodes.
我当时看过几集。

475
00:18:53.020 --> 00:18:57.980
My friend Sam had them recorded from someone in England on a VHS.
我朋友萨姆通过英国的朋友用录像带录了下来。

476
00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:00.720
It was before they were like available in the United States.
那是在美国还没引进之前。

477
00:19:00.860 --> 00:19:01.820
It was really early on.
那是很早的时候了。

478
00:19:02.180 --> 00:19:04.440
I had seen them and I just loved them.
我看过，而且非常喜欢。

479
00:19:04.580 --> 00:19:08.080
And I, and inside and outside, I was like, oh, that's great.
我当时由衷地觉得，哦，那太棒了。

480
00:19:08.240 --> 00:19:08.520
That's great.
太棒了。

481
00:19:12.820 --> 00:19:14.280
That show's so awesome.
那部剧真是太赞了。

482
00:19:16.120 --> 00:19:18.300
And so I was like, okay, see you later.
所以我说，好的，回头见。

483
00:19:18.580 --> 00:19:19.480
Went to the table read.
去了剧本围读现场。

484
00:19:19.620 --> 00:19:22.460
This is one of the most incredible experiences.
这是我经历过最不可思议的事情之一。

485
00:19:22.700 --> 00:19:25.520
In fact, Kent Zvornak was the producer on it.
事实上，肯特·兹沃纳克是那部剧的制片人。

486
00:19:25.740 --> 00:19:26.760
Oh my gosh.
天哪。

487
00:19:26.860 --> 00:19:27.120
Wow.
哇。

488
00:19:27.220 --> 00:19:27.700
Kentopedia?
肯特百科全书？

489
00:19:28.180 --> 00:19:28.520
Yeah.
是的。

490
00:19:28.820 --> 00:19:31.800
So we did the table read and this was an infamous event.
我们进行了剧本围读，那是一次臭名昭著的事件。

491
00:19:32.040 --> 00:19:32.860
We did the table read.
我们读了剧本。

492
00:19:32.960 --> 00:19:37.800
It went so bad that the plug was pulled immediately.
结果太糟糕了，项目立刻就被叫停了。

493
00:19:38.200 --> 00:19:39.140
They canceled it?
他们取消了？

494
00:19:39.260 --> 00:19:40.400
They didn't, you didn't even shoot it?
他们没拍？你甚至还没开始拍？

495
00:19:41.060 --> 00:19:42.100
I did not shoot it.
我没拍成。

496
00:19:42.100 --> 00:19:43.220
They had sets built.
他们连布景都搭好了。

497
00:19:43.460 --> 00:19:44.740
We had plane tickets.
我们机票都买好了。

498
00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:46.820
We had hotel rooms booked.
酒店房间也订好了。

499
00:19:47.340 --> 00:19:51.360
I was supposed to fly the next morning and then start shooting in like two days.
我本该第二天早上飞过去，然后两天后开拍。

500
00:19:51.760 --> 00:19:53.640
And the table read went so poorly.
结果剧本围读的效果太差了。

501
00:19:53.920 --> 00:19:55.540
We found the name, by the way.
顺便说一下，我们找到了那个名字。

502
00:19:55.660 --> 00:19:57.460
The name is Slice O' Life.
名字叫《Slice O' Life》。

503
00:19:58.100 --> 00:19:59.200
Slice O' Life.
《Slice O' Life》。

504
00:19:59.380 --> 00:20:01.660
That's what I knew it had life in it and an S.
我就知道它里面有“life”和一个“S”。

505
00:20:03.580 --> 00:20:06.080
But so all of a sudden I was free to do the office.
但突然之间，我有空去试镜《办公室》了。

506
00:20:06.280 --> 00:20:07.420
So I called my agent.
所以我给经纪人打了电话。

507
00:20:07.520 --> 00:20:09.320
I was like, I'd really like to audition for this office.
我说，我真的很想去试镜这部剧。

508
00:20:09.320 --> 00:20:14.500
And yes, I was, I was the first person to audition on the very first day.
没错，我是第一天第一个去试镜的人。

509
00:20:14.660 --> 00:20:18.820
Alison Jones, the casting director, kind of knew me from Six Feet Under and some other things.
选角导演艾莉森·琼斯因为《六英尺下》和其他一些作品对我有点印象。

510
00:20:18.900 --> 00:20:20.280
I was so excited.
我当时太兴奋了。

511
00:20:20.280 --> 00:20:25.020
And I auditioned for both Dwight and Michael on that first day.
那天我同时试镜了德怀特和迈克尔这两个角色。

512
00:20:25.360 --> 00:20:29.580
And she keeps threatening to release my Michael Scott audition.
她一直威胁说要放出我试镜迈克尔·斯科特的录像。

513
00:20:29.860 --> 00:20:34.660
It is truly terrible because I just did a Ricky Gervais impersonation.
那真的太糟糕了，因为我当时只是在模仿瑞奇·热维斯。

514
00:20:34.840 --> 00:20:36.660
I didn't know what else to do.
我不知道还能怎么演。

515
00:20:36.660 --> 00:20:39.380
So I was kind of pulling on my tie a lot.
所以我一直在不停地扯领带。

516
00:20:39.520 --> 00:20:45.120
And it was, but Dwight, I knew, I was like, this is completely in my wheelhouse.
但对于德怀特，我当时就觉得，这完全是我的拿手好戏。

517
00:20:45.600 --> 00:20:48.100
I know exactly who this person is.
我非常清楚这个人是谁。

518
00:20:48.380 --> 00:20:50.020
This guy is in my DNA.
这个家伙就在我的基因里。

519
00:20:50.320 --> 00:20:54.860
I have cousins who are really not that different from Dwight Schrute.
我有几个表亲和德怀特·舒特真的没多大区别。

520
00:20:55.340 --> 00:20:57.620
And the rest is history.
剩下的就是历史了。

521
00:20:58.440 --> 00:21:02.820
Well, Rain, I remember being paired with you during the screen tests.
雷恩，我记得在试镜时和你搭档过。

522
00:21:03.720 --> 00:21:06.160
And they were mixing and matching us.
当时他们把我们混在一起配对。

523
00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:10.760
There were like four Pams and four Jims and four Dwights and a few Michaels.
大概有四个帕姆、四个吉姆、四个德怀特和几个迈克尔。

524
00:21:11.020 --> 00:21:19.840
Bob Odenkirk was one of the Michaels, which is so crazy because I guess he was available as well since Slice O' Life didn't go forward.
鲍勃·奥登科克就是其中一个迈克尔，这太疯狂了，我想是因为《Slice O' Life》没能继续，所以他也有档期。

525
00:21:20.120 --> 00:21:21.840
And Ken Zmanack was available.
肯·兹马纳克当时也有档期。

526
00:21:22.200 --> 00:21:22.480
Yeah.
没错。

527
00:21:22.700 --> 00:21:22.900
Wow.
哇。

528
00:21:22.980 --> 00:21:25.680
We really got a lot of folks from Slice O' Life.
我们真的从《Slice O' Life》剧组挖来了不少人。

529
00:21:25.840 --> 00:21:26.660
We got lucky there.
我们运气真好。

530
00:21:26.840 --> 00:21:27.500
We scored.
我们赚到了。

531
00:21:27.500 --> 00:21:30.300
But Rain, I remember being paired with you.
但雷恩，我记得当时和你搭档。

532
00:21:31.420 --> 00:21:34.380
And I mean, I couldn't believe it.
我是说，我简直不敢相信。

533
00:21:34.520 --> 00:21:41.660
Of all of us, of all of us, you were 100% there from the beginning.
在我们所有人中，你从一开始就百分之百进入了状态。

534
00:21:42.000 --> 00:21:46.080
I feel like from that moment that I did that first audition scene with you.
我觉得从我和你演第一场试镜戏的那一刻起就是这样。

535
00:21:46.380 --> 00:21:49.140
Everybody else, I was paired with John.
至于其他人，我当时是和约翰搭档的。

536
00:21:49.140 --> 00:21:51.180
And I was like, oh, yeah, this is great.
我当时想，哦，太棒了。

537
00:21:51.340 --> 00:21:53.180
And Steve and everybody.
还有史蒂夫和其他所有人。

538
00:21:53.180 --> 00:22:01.580
But Rain, you were just like, I didn't even know where Rain began and Dwight ended or Dwight began and Rain ended.
但雷恩，你当时的状态，我甚至分不清哪里是雷恩，哪里是德怀特，或者哪里是德怀特，哪里是雷恩。

539
00:22:01.720 --> 00:22:02.860
I mean, it was so fluid.
我是说，那种感觉太自然了。

540
00:22:03.180 --> 00:22:04.240
It was amazing.
太神奇了。

541
00:22:04.940 --> 00:22:08.400
But you were, I have to say, there's a mutual admiration society.
但我必须说，我们是互相欣赏的。

542
00:22:08.840 --> 00:22:12.880
For those who don't know, Jenna was totally in Pam, dressed as Pam.
对于那些不知道的人，珍娜当时完全沉浸在帕姆的角色里，打扮得就像帕姆一样。

543
00:22:13.260 --> 00:22:19.240
You were reading the book on John Belushi, Wired, that you thought Pam would be reading.
你当时在读那本关于约翰·贝鲁西的书《Wired》，你觉得帕姆会读那本书。

544
00:22:19.520 --> 00:22:21.640
It was in the script that she was reading it.
剧本里写了她正在读那本书。

545
00:22:21.640 --> 00:22:22.980
So I read the whole novel.
所以我把整本书都读完了。

546
00:22:23.260 --> 00:22:24.520
I read the whole thing.
我把它全读完了。

547
00:22:24.520 --> 00:22:26.660
I was like, my character read it.
我当时想，我的角色读过它。

548
00:22:26.800 --> 00:22:27.360
I'll read it.
那我也得读。

549
00:22:28.400 --> 00:22:28.880
Yeah.
没错。

550
00:22:29.860 --> 00:22:32.660
And you were Pam in the waiting room, too.
而且你在候场室里也一直保持着帕姆的状态。

551
00:22:34.100 --> 00:22:35.660
But that was so much fun.
但那真的太有趣了。

552
00:22:35.860 --> 00:22:46.140
And we had, I don't know if they'd ever released that audition, but that improvisation where I was just sitting, I was kneeling like way too close to you.
而且我们当时，我不知道他们有没有发布过那段试镜，但我当时即兴表演时，我就坐在那儿，跪得离你太近了。

553
00:22:46.140 --> 00:22:46.520
Yeah.
是啊。

554
00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:52.560
Like, which is something I love to do as Dwight is like, he doesn't have an understanding of like, personal space.
就像，这是我作为德怀特很喜欢做的一件事，他完全没有那种个人空间的概念。

555
00:22:52.640 --> 00:22:53.400
He does not.
他确实没有。

556
00:22:53.700 --> 00:22:56.580
He could be talking to someone like four inches away from them.
他可以跟人说话时离对方只有四英寸远。

557
00:22:56.780 --> 00:22:58.640
And I thought, I always thought that was really funny.
我觉得，我一直觉得那特别好笑。

558
00:23:00.380 --> 00:23:04.260
And where I talked about my girlfriend being stationed in Kuwait.
还有我提到我女朋友驻扎在科威特的时候。

559
00:23:07.200 --> 00:23:08.860
And that was very funny.
那段也非常搞笑。

560
00:23:09.100 --> 00:23:13.340
And you just, and it was such a great improv because most actors feel like, oh, I'm improv-ing.
你当时，那真是一段很棒的即兴表演，因为大多数演员会觉得，哦，我在即兴表演。

561
00:23:13.500 --> 00:23:14.960
I need to talk a lot.
我得说很多话。

562
00:23:15.240 --> 00:23:18.920
You know, they think like, oh, improvisation means talking a lot.
你知道，他们觉得，哦，即兴表演就是多说话。

563
00:23:18.920 --> 00:23:31.560
And this was an improv where I kind of did this monologue and you just gazed painfully into space, taking in my body odor and my proximity and the strangeness of my story.
而这次即兴表演里，我说了那段独白，而你只是痛苦地凝视着虚空，忍受着我的体味、我的近距离接触，还有我那故事的怪异感。

564
00:23:32.080 --> 00:23:33.780
And it was, it was fantastic.
那真是太棒了。

565
00:23:34.040 --> 00:23:37.000
And when we did that, I was like, oh, I know that we're going to have these parts.
当我们做完那段表演时，我就想，哦，我知道我们肯定会拿到这些角色了。

566
00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:37.940
Yeah.
是啊。

567
00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:39.180
I felt that way, too.
我当时也有这种感觉。

568
00:23:39.280 --> 00:23:43.300
And I felt at that audition, it was very clear to me that you were their choice.
而且在那次试镜中，我非常清楚你就是他们的人选。

569
00:23:44.740 --> 00:23:46.800
Did they keep pairing different people with Rain?
他们当时是不是一直在给雷恩搭配不同的人？

570
00:23:46.960 --> 00:23:47.900
Because that's how you know.
因为那就是你判断的方式。

571
00:23:47.900 --> 00:23:52.580
You know that's the person when they're like, oh, let's see him with this person and this person and this person.
当他们说，哦，让我们看看他和这个人、那个人、还有那个人搭戏效果如何时，你就知道那个人就是最终人选了。

572
00:23:52.760 --> 00:23:54.480
And I only got paired with him once.
我只和他搭档过一次。

573
00:23:54.480 --> 00:23:59.080
And that made me a little nervous because it was very clear to me that Rain had the part.
这让我有点紧张，因为我很清楚雷恩已经拿到了那个角色。

574
00:23:59.740 --> 00:24:02.060
And so I was like, oh, well, I'll pair with him again.
所以我当时想，哦，好吧，我再和他搭档一次吧。

575
00:24:02.060 --> 00:24:04.280
Yeah, they mostly matched me with a lot of different gyMs.
是啊，他们主要是让我和很多不同的吉姆搭档。

576
00:24:04.460 --> 00:24:06.420
I remember reading with a lot of different gyMs.
我记得我和很多不同的吉姆一起读过剧本。

577
00:24:06.540 --> 00:24:06.720
Yeah.
是啊。

578
00:24:07.460 --> 00:24:16.960
And the reason they said ultimately they went with John, I mean, obviously he's charming and handsome and funny and great deadpan and smart as hell.
他们说最终选择约翰的原因，我是说，显然他很有魅力、长得帅、风趣幽默、冷面笑匠功力深厚，而且聪明绝顶。

579
00:24:16.960 --> 00:24:18.240
And like a ball.
而且像个球一样。

580
00:24:18.880 --> 00:24:21.880
But that his size was comparable to mine.
但他的体型和我相当。

581
00:24:22.080 --> 00:24:24.720
There were a couple other gyms that were like five foot seven.
还有几个吉姆大概只有五英尺七英寸高。

582
00:24:25.200 --> 00:24:28.360
And it just seemed like Dwight would just overpower them.
看起来德怀特会完全压制住他们。

583
00:24:28.600 --> 00:24:30.300
The gym was actually taller than me.
那个吉姆其实比我还高。

584
00:24:30.500 --> 00:24:34.580
So we kind of like we really matched up kind of energy wise.
所以我们在能量上真的很匹配。

585
00:24:35.060 --> 00:24:36.600
That makes sense to me.
这对我来说很有道理。

586
00:24:36.760 --> 00:24:37.720
Yeah, that does.
是啊，确实如此。

587
00:24:37.920 --> 00:24:43.060
But then they went a whole other way with your romantic life and they picked the tiniest person in the office.
但后来他们在你的感情生活上走了完全不同的路，选了办公室里最娇小的人。

588
00:24:44.440 --> 00:24:46.740
Tiniest, tiniest little sprig.
最娇小、最娇小的一小枝。

589
00:24:47.060 --> 00:24:50.860
Yeah, but I didn't think they knew that Dwight and Angela were going to get together.
是啊，但我认为他们当时并不知道德怀特和安吉拉会走到一起。

590
00:24:51.020 --> 00:24:51.520
They just were.
他们只是顺其自然。

591
00:24:52.020 --> 00:24:56.560
I don't know where that storyline came from, but I imagine they were just kind of floundering in season two.
我不知道那条故事线是怎么来的，但我猜他们第二季时可能有点不知所措。

592
00:24:56.720 --> 00:24:57.860
Like, oh, we got to mix things up.
就像，哦，我们得搞点新花样。

593
00:24:57.860 --> 00:25:01.300
Like, because at first they had me together with Kelly.
因为起初他们让我和凯莉在一起。

594
00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:03.000
They had me kiss Kelly Kapoor.
他们让我吻了凯莉·卡普尔。

595
00:25:03.620 --> 00:25:05.120
But Angela was furious.
但安吉拉当时气疯了。

596
00:25:05.800 --> 00:25:07.780
Angela watched it and was furious.
安吉拉看了那一幕，气得不行。

597
00:25:09.260 --> 00:25:14.900
Remember, they had me like look in the camera like they made me look so like they kept saying more anger, more.
记得吗，他们让我盯着镜头看，他们让我表现得，他们一直说再愤怒一点，再愤怒一点。

598
00:25:15.080 --> 00:25:17.300
I was like, oh, my God, my eyes are going to pop out of my head.
我当时想，天哪，我的眼珠都要瞪出来了。

599
00:25:18.400 --> 00:25:21.000
But I think I think our writers just sat there.
但我认为，我认为我们的编剧当时只是坐在那儿。

600
00:25:21.100 --> 00:25:23.620
Jenna and I have talked about this and we've talked to our writers about it,
我和珍娜讨论过这件事，我们也和编剧聊过。

601
00:25:23.700 --> 00:25:32.900
how they would just take two names and put them on a card and just see what that felt like and sort of spitball a little bit about what those two people would bring out of each other.
他们会把两个名字写在卡片上，看看会有什么感觉，然后即兴探讨一下这两个人碰撞在一起会产生什么样的火花。

602
00:25:33.620 --> 00:25:33.800
Right.
没错。

603
00:25:34.260 --> 00:25:37.360
And that is one thing that Greg talked about.
这也是格雷格提到过的一点。

604
00:25:37.360 --> 00:25:41.660
And I remember, and it's really great lesson for comedy writers and screenwriters.
我记得，这对喜剧编剧和剧本作家来说真的是一个很好的经验。

605
00:25:41.840 --> 00:25:49.860
He said a lot of shows really focus on a character and like, oh, let's make this character really specific and funny and interesting.
他说很多剧集都专注于塑造一个角色，比如，哦，让我们把这个角色写得特别、有趣且引人入胜。

606
00:25:50.120 --> 00:25:55.960
But he was really about like when these two two characters bang up against each other.
但他更看重的是当这两个角色发生碰撞时会怎样。

607
00:25:56.540 --> 00:25:57.600
That's what she said.
她就是这么说的。

608
00:25:57.860 --> 00:25:59.340
Then what do what happens?
那之后会发生什么呢？

609
00:25:59.800 --> 00:26:02.040
What happens with that energy?
那种能量会产生什么结果？

610
00:26:02.300 --> 00:26:06.400
You know, so it was more about he was much more about dynamics between characters.
你知道，他更关注的是角色之间的互动关系。

611
00:26:06.400 --> 00:26:09.060
And I think that's one of the successes of the office.
我认为这也是《办公室》成功的原因之一。

612
00:26:09.920 --> 00:26:17.980
Well, this episode that we're talking about today, Golden Ticket, has a classic Michael Dwight pairing.
我们今天讨论的这一集《金奖券》，就有迈克尔和德怀特这对经典组合。

613
00:26:18.940 --> 00:26:29.720
And we just I love in this rewatch watching the way that Dwight can be both Michael's lackey and then also like you can take him to task.
在这次重温中，我特别喜欢看德怀特如何既能当迈克尔的跟班，又能对他进行指责。

614
00:26:29.900 --> 00:26:30.880
You stand up to him.
你敢于反抗他。

615
00:26:31.720 --> 00:26:33.600
What was that like for you?
这对你来说是什么样的体验？

616
00:26:33.600 --> 00:26:39.820
You were in this comedy duo with Steve Carell for seven years, playing out moments like this.
你和史蒂夫·卡瑞尔搭档了七年的喜剧二人组，演绎过很多这样的时刻。

617
00:26:40.360 --> 00:26:41.560
What was that experience?
那段经历是怎样的？

618
00:26:43.300 --> 00:26:45.460
Well, that's a bunch of questions.
好吧，你这一连问了好几个问题。

619
00:26:45.700 --> 00:26:49.020
And I know I that's how I like to interview people.
我知道，我采访别人时也喜欢这样。

620
00:26:49.160 --> 00:26:56.040
She just likes to throw like 13 big, overarching, like huge questions all at once.
她就是喜欢一下子抛出十三个宏大、概括性的重磅问题。

621
00:26:56.540 --> 00:26:57.360
I love it.
我喜欢这样。

622
00:26:57.560 --> 00:26:58.780
Well, let's let me hit that one.
好吧，让我来回答那个问题。

623
00:26:58.860 --> 00:27:13.420
Let me just say that, you know, when I look back on that work with Steve, I'm just so grateful because he's obviously like one of the greateSt.
我想说的是，当我回首与史蒂夫共事的时光，我感到非常感激，因为他显然是史上最伟大的演员之一。

624
00:27:14.660 --> 00:27:18.660
Actors, comedy actors, but even just actors like ever.
喜剧演员，甚至可以说是史上最伟大的演员之一。

625
00:27:18.660 --> 00:27:24.660
And the fact that I got to do so much work with him was just such a gift.
能和他有那么多的合作，对我来说真是一份厚礼。

626
00:27:25.260 --> 00:27:27.380
I didn't come from an improv background.
我并非出身于即兴表演背景。

627
00:27:27.620 --> 00:27:33.520
I was always good at improv, but I went to theater school and I did Shakespeare and I did Eugene O'Neill.
我一直擅长即兴表演，但我上的是戏剧学校，演过莎士比亚和尤金·奥尼尔的作品。

628
00:27:33.660 --> 00:27:38.220
And I was in New York kind of off off Broadway theater guy.
我以前在纽约是个演外外百老汇戏剧的演员。

629
00:27:38.220 --> 00:27:41.980
And Steve was from Second City and had done years and years and years of improv.
而史蒂夫来自“第二城”剧团，有多年即兴表演的经验。

630
00:27:42.220 --> 00:27:44.440
So that was his thing.
所以那是他的强项。

631
00:27:46.200 --> 00:27:49.500
But the thing about Steve that, you know, they always have this.
但关于史蒂夫，你知道，人们总是提到这一点。

632
00:27:49.620 --> 00:27:51.380
It's kind of become a cliche, like the yes.
这已经成了一种陈词滥调，比如“是的，而且”。

633
00:27:51.600 --> 00:27:53.320
And, you know, like an improv.
你知道，就像在即兴表演中那样。

634
00:27:53.580 --> 00:27:59.680
If you say like, hey, you know, I bought a pet peacock.
如果你说，嘿，我买了一只宠物孔雀。

635
00:28:02.000 --> 00:28:03.380
Then you say yes.
然后对方会说，是的。

636
00:28:03.580 --> 00:28:05.680
And like, oh, I'd love to see it.
而且，哦，我很想看看它。

637
00:28:05.780 --> 00:28:07.460
Can I feed it my mealworms or whatever?
我能喂它吃我的面包虫或者别的什么吗？

638
00:28:08.220 --> 00:28:10.340
And Steve was incredible at that.
史蒂夫在这方面简直太棒了。

639
00:28:10.480 --> 00:28:11.620
No matter what I did.
无论我做什么。

640
00:28:12.980 --> 00:28:15.520
And sometimes I would try to go really out of the box.
有时我会尝试跳出框架。

641
00:28:16.000 --> 00:28:24.080
Steve would completely react in character and accept what was being proposed.
史蒂夫会完全以角色的身份做出反应，并接受所提出的设定。

642
00:28:24.520 --> 00:28:28.320
So I could just in the because obviously we would we would shoot a scene.
所以我可以在……因为显然我们会拍摄一场戏。

643
00:28:28.680 --> 00:28:29.760
We would improvise.
我们会进行即兴发挥。

644
00:28:30.380 --> 00:28:31.740
I mean, we would do the script.
我是说，我们会按照剧本演。

645
00:28:31.880 --> 00:28:34.460
We would shoot the script and make sure we got it scripted correctly.
我们会拍摄剧本内容，确保剧本部分拍摄准确。

646
00:28:34.860 --> 00:28:36.380
And then we would could improvise.
然后我们就可以进行即兴表演了。

647
00:28:36.380 --> 00:28:40.040
And then sometimes it would just we just freely improvise and just go off.
有时我们甚至会完全自由地即兴发挥，随心所欲。

648
00:28:40.040 --> 00:28:48.500
And I remember just being like I could say something like I decided to open a llama farm just out of nowhere or something.
我记得我当时会突然说些什么，比如我决定开一个羊驼农场，完全是突如其来的。

649
00:28:48.620 --> 00:28:53.680
And Steve would just listen as Michael take that in and be like, wait, what are you talking about?
史蒂夫会以迈克尔的身份倾听，接受这个设定，然后说，等等，你在说什么？

650
00:28:54.140 --> 00:28:54.580
Llamas?
羊驼？

651
00:28:54.580 --> 00:28:56.760
What what does that have to do with anything?
这这跟那有什么关系吗？

652
00:28:57.100 --> 00:28:57.440
Why?
为什么？

653
00:28:58.180 --> 00:28:59.700
You're so weird, Dwight.
你真奇怪，德怀特。

654
00:28:59.880 --> 00:29:00.680
Oh, go away.
噢，走开。

655
00:29:00.780 --> 00:29:01.140
You're icky.
你真讨厌。

656
00:29:01.580 --> 00:29:04.600
Like and it would just be completely in the moment.
就像是完全沉浸在当下的那一刻。

657
00:29:04.600 --> 00:29:09.200
And I just learned so much from that process.
而且我从那个过程中学到了很多。

658
00:29:10.160 --> 00:29:13.840
He never got kind of like, God damn it, Rain.
他从来不会表现出那种“该死，雷恩”的感觉。

659
00:29:13.980 --> 00:29:15.980
Why are you being so weird and so silly?
你为什么要表现得这么奇怪又这么傻？

660
00:29:16.180 --> 00:29:17.720
Like stay on the point of the scene.
就像是紧扣场景的主题一样。

661
00:29:17.900 --> 00:29:23.460
And we can go way off kilter, you know, way off the path.
我们可以偏离主题很远，你知道的，完全偏离轨道。

662
00:29:23.600 --> 00:29:26.920
And he would just be right there all the time.
而他总是能一直待在那里。

663
00:29:26.920 --> 00:29:30.060
It was really a privilege to work with him.
能和他一起工作真是我的荣幸。

664
00:29:31.500 --> 00:29:37.840
I loved it when there'd be a conference room scene and clearly Michael had an agenda and things to say.
我特别喜欢会议室的场景，迈克尔显然有自己的议程和想说的话。

665
00:29:38.340 --> 00:29:41.640
And you you as Dwight, of all people, would interject.
而你，作为德怀特，竟然会插话。

666
00:29:42.060 --> 00:29:42.200
Right.
没错。

667
00:29:43.120 --> 00:29:49.900
And Rain, so many times I go to the script to see if it was written or improvised because I feel like I can tell now.
雷恩，我好多次去看剧本，想看看那是写好的还是即兴发挥的，因为我觉得我现在能分辨出来了。

668
00:29:50.700 --> 00:29:52.780
And they're always so good.
而且它们总是那么精彩。

669
00:29:52.880 --> 00:29:54.840
But but it's like seamless.
但这就像是天衣无缝的。

670
00:29:54.840 --> 00:29:58.920
You would never know because of exactly what you just shared, because Steve is Michael.
你永远不会知道，就像你刚才分享的那样，因为史蒂夫就是迈克尔。

671
00:29:59.140 --> 00:30:03.820
No matter what you piped up and said, just like would just take it and run with it.
无论你插嘴说了什么，他都能接住并顺着演下去。

672
00:30:04.080 --> 00:30:08.000
And it was always like an absolute joy.
那真是一种绝对的乐趣。

673
00:30:08.200 --> 00:30:08.620
You know me.
你了解我的。

674
00:30:08.740 --> 00:30:10.500
I'm a nerdy, nerdy improv gal.
我是一个书呆子式的即兴表演爱好者。

675
00:30:10.500 --> 00:30:15.120
Well, we've talked on the podcast that you and Jenna had your whole like we did theater.
嗯，我们在播客里聊过，你和珍娜你们俩有那种“我们演过戏”的经历。

676
00:30:15.900 --> 00:30:19.320
And Jenna likes to remind me of it, Rain, much like you did.
珍娜喜欢提醒我这一点，雷恩，就像你刚才做的那样。

677
00:30:20.440 --> 00:30:26.540
But as like a nerdy improv gal watching you guys, it was it was just awesome.
但作为一个看着你们表演的书呆子即兴爱好者，这真是太棒了。

678
00:30:26.820 --> 00:30:30.060
I felt like I had a front row seat of just some really magical moments.
我觉得自己就像坐在前排，亲眼见证了一些真正神奇的时刻。

679
00:30:30.560 --> 00:30:32.940
And getting specifically to Golden Ticket.
专门说到《金奖券》这一集。

680
00:30:33.300 --> 00:30:33.900
Thank you, Angela.
谢谢你，安吉拉。

681
00:30:34.340 --> 00:30:38.680
And but yeah, I hadn't seen this one since it came out.
而且，是的，自从这一集播出后我就没再看过。

682
00:30:38.680 --> 00:30:42.480
And it was so fun to watch.
看这一集真的很有趣。

683
00:30:42.780 --> 00:30:53.860
And Jenna, just like you said, that dynamic of Dwight being toady, lackey, suck up, just so desperate for Michael's approval.
珍娜，就像你说的，德怀特那种马屁精、走狗、奉承者的动态，是那么渴望得到迈克尔的认可。

684
00:30:55.260 --> 00:30:59.320
And then oddly, realizing he's got some power here.
然后奇怪的是，他意识到自己在这里也有了一些权力。

685
00:31:00.760 --> 00:31:08.460
And, you know, that switch when he's shaking David Wallace's hand and he says, you know, thank you and takes the credit for it.
你知道的，当他握住大卫·华莱士的手说“谢谢你”并把功劳揽到自己身上时，那种转变。

686
00:31:08.460 --> 00:31:15.180
And then Steve's expression of it was so priceless of like, oh, that guy.
还有史蒂夫当时那种无价的表情，仿佛在说“噢，这家伙”。

687
00:31:16.000 --> 00:31:23.880
And then your fight in the marketing meeting, like when you get on the phone with the marketing guys, the two of you back and forth with your big ideas.
还有你们在营销会议上的争吵，比如当你和营销人员通电话时，你们俩来回抛出那些宏大的想法。

688
00:31:24.640 --> 00:31:33.360
Yeah, horse boats and all the toilet, toilet, toilet net is a lot of toilet ideas.
没错，马船，还有各种厕所，厕所，厕所网，真的是一堆关于厕所的点子。

689
00:31:34.280 --> 00:31:35.380
You don't have ideas.
你根本没什么点子。

690
00:31:35.500 --> 00:31:36.100
Yes, I do.
不，我有。

691
00:31:38.340 --> 00:31:44.460
So I would love to see an extended cut of that because I bet that there were a lot more ideas we tossed back and forth in that scene.
所以我很想看那一幕的加长版，因为我敢打赌，我们在那场戏里还来回抛出了更多点子。

692
00:31:44.780 --> 00:31:50.600
We should ask Dave Rogers, the keeper of all of the extra footage, because I bet you're right.
我们应该问问戴夫·罗杰斯，他是所有额外素材的保管人，因为我敢打赌你是对的。

693
00:31:50.800 --> 00:31:52.140
There had to have been even more.
肯定还有更多。

694
00:31:52.140 --> 00:32:02.300
Also, this one was written by Mindy Kaling, and she was amazing at coming up with on the fly, in the moment, extra stuff to hand you.
另外，这一集是敏迪·卡灵写的，她非常擅长在现场即兴想出额外的点子递给你。

695
00:32:02.520 --> 00:32:08.600
I have to tell you guys, in the script, I reread it, Pam tries to butt in with an idea.
我得告诉你们，在剧本里，我重读了一遍，帕姆试图插话提一个点子。

696
00:32:09.020 --> 00:32:09.300
What?
什么？

697
00:32:09.640 --> 00:32:10.120
Yes.
是的。

698
00:32:10.340 --> 00:32:13.880
And Michael and Dwight shoot her down.
然后迈克尔和德怀特把她怼了回去。

699
00:32:14.000 --> 00:32:17.340
It's the one thing they agree on is that Pam's idea is so stupid.
他们唯一达成一致的事情就是帕姆的点子太蠢了。

700
00:32:17.340 --> 00:32:23.600
She says, as they're yelling all their ideas, Pam meekly just says, remote control toilets.
当他们大喊着各自的点子时，帕姆怯生生地说了一句：遥控马桶。

701
00:32:23.920 --> 00:32:25.520
And they're both like, nah, it's stupid.
他们俩都觉得，不，这太蠢了。

702
00:32:25.620 --> 00:32:26.220
Doesn't make sense.
根本说不通。

703
00:32:26.360 --> 00:32:26.700
It's dumb.
太傻了。

704
00:32:28.940 --> 00:32:29.600
That's great.
那太棒了。

705
00:32:29.620 --> 00:32:30.740
I wish they would have kept that.
我真希望他们当时能留着那个。

706
00:32:30.860 --> 00:32:31.360
That's great.
那太棒了。

707
00:32:32.400 --> 00:32:34.920
We have another question that we've never asked you, Rain.
雷恩，我们还有一个从未问过你的问题。

708
00:32:36.080 --> 00:32:38.420
This is a popular one we ask all our guests.
这是我们问所有嘉宾的一个热门问题。

709
00:32:38.980 --> 00:32:39.200
Okay.
好的。

710
00:32:39.680 --> 00:32:42.140
Did you take anything from set when the show wrapped?
剧集杀青时，你从片场拿走什么东西了吗？

711
00:32:43.640 --> 00:32:45.160
Oh, this breaks my heart.
噢，这真让我心碎。

712
00:32:45.160 --> 00:32:48.200
Um, I should have taken so much more.
嗯，我本该多拿些东西的。

713
00:32:48.300 --> 00:32:50.380
I should have fleeced NBC Universal.
我当时就该把NBC环球给洗劫一空。

714
00:32:51.020 --> 00:32:53.820
Um, I took Dwight's glasses.
嗯，我拿走了德怀特的眼镜。

715
00:32:53.940 --> 00:32:57.360
I took his little desk plate that said Dwight Schrute on it.
我拿走了他桌上写着“德怀特·施鲁特”的小名牌。

716
00:32:57.800 --> 00:32:59.220
I took his stapler.
我拿走了他的订书机。

717
00:33:01.220 --> 00:33:04.980
And one or two other things I can't quite remember.
还有一两件其他东西，我记不太清了。

718
00:33:04.980 --> 00:33:06.460
I have to look around and see.
我得四处找找看。

719
00:33:07.080 --> 00:33:10.520
But I had a whole list of things I gave to Phil Shea.
但我当时列了一长串清单给菲尔·谢伊。

720
00:33:10.840 --> 00:33:13.340
And I said, Phil, pull these aside for me.
我对他说，菲尔，把这些帮我留出来。

721
00:33:13.980 --> 00:33:15.400
And I'll get them from you later.
我回头再找你拿。

722
00:33:16.140 --> 00:33:21.840
And it was, you know, Dwight's briefcase and this and that and the other thing and blah,
当时就是，你知道，德怀特的公文包，这个那个，还有别的什么东西，巴拉巴拉的。

723
00:33:21.900 --> 00:33:22.160
blah, blah.
巴拉巴拉。

724
00:33:22.160 --> 00:33:25.100
And, um, and Phil was like, okay.
然后，嗯，菲尔说，好的。

725
00:33:25.240 --> 00:33:31.410
And then I went back to Phil and he's like, I couldn't get them.
后来我再去找菲尔，他说，我没能拿到那些东西。

726
00:33:31.690 --> 00:33:32.390
Sorry, blah, blah, blah.
抱歉，巴拉巴拉的。

727
00:33:32.570 --> 00:33:33.970
And then I heard from someone else.
后来我从别人那儿听说。

728
00:33:34.130 --> 00:33:39.990
They were like, oh, they threatened the crew to be fired and never worked for NBC Universal again.
他们说，噢，他们威胁剧组人员，如果被发现从办公室拿走任何东西，就会被开除，而且永远别想再为NBC环球工作。

729
00:33:39.990 --> 00:33:45.610
If they caught them taking anything from the office.
如果他们抓到谁拿了办公室的东西。

730
00:33:46.570 --> 00:33:48.570
And we didn't know why.
我们当时都不知道为什么。

731
00:33:48.850 --> 00:33:54.070
And then they had that big auction where they auctioned all this stuff off on eBay.
后来他们搞了一场大型拍卖会，把这些东西全在eBay上拍卖了。

732
00:33:54.610 --> 00:33:57.310
You know, even like Dwight's desk was auctioned off.
你知道，连德怀特的办公桌都被拍卖了。

733
00:33:57.510 --> 00:33:59.470
Did you not get your bobblehead?
你没拿到你的摇头娃娃吗？

734
00:34:01.010 --> 00:34:06.010
I got one of the rejected bobbleheads that doesn't look anything like the bobblehead.
我拿到了一个被淘汰的摇头娃娃，长得一点都不像那个娃娃。

735
00:34:06.110 --> 00:34:07.770
I did not get my original bobblehead.
我没拿到我原本的那个摇头娃娃。

736
00:34:07.990 --> 00:34:08.070
No.
没有。

737
00:34:08.350 --> 00:34:08.890
I see.
我明白了。

738
00:34:09.510 --> 00:34:10.150
That's a shame.
那真是太可惜了。

739
00:34:10.150 --> 00:34:14.110
And I have to feel shame for the painting, the Dwight painting that's kind of where he's
我还得为那幅画感到遗憾，就是那幅德怀特的画，他看起来有点像

740
00:34:14.110 --> 00:34:15.010
like Chairman Mao.
毛主席的那幅。

741
00:34:15.330 --> 00:34:15.490
Yeah, yeah.
是啊，是啊。

742
00:34:16.590 --> 00:34:18.970
And, um, that didn't happen either.
嗯，那幅画我也没拿到。

743
00:34:19.570 --> 00:34:23.550
Well, Rain, you know, you've gone on to do so many awesome things, but we would love to
好吧，雷恩，你知道，你后来做了很多很棒的事情，但我们很想

744
00:34:23.550 --> 00:34:27.130
talk to you about your podcast, Metaphysical Milkshake.
和你聊聊你的播客《形而上学的奶昔》。

745
00:34:27.350 --> 00:34:32.170
I listened to a great episode last night when, um, you had Mike Schur on.
昨晚我听了很棒的一期，嗯，你请来了迈克·舒尔。

746
00:34:32.970 --> 00:34:33.410
Yeah.
是的。

747
00:34:33.910 --> 00:34:35.570
And that was so amazing.
那期节目太精彩了。

748
00:34:35.570 --> 00:34:37.830
Just talking about what is good, what is bad.
就是讨论什么是善，什么是恶。

749
00:34:37.830 --> 00:34:41.310
And he sort of like folded in his show, The Good Place into that episode.
他还在那期节目里融入了他的剧集《善地》。

750
00:34:41.310 --> 00:34:46.430
But you and Reza are so thoughtful and you're really asking life's big questions.
你和礼萨真的很有思想，你们探讨的都是人生的大问题。

751
00:34:46.430 --> 00:34:48.270
And it's a great listen.
而且这节目非常值得一听。

752
00:34:49.790 --> 00:34:50.470
Yeah, thanks.
是啊，谢谢。

753
00:34:50.650 --> 00:34:54.350
Well, you guys know this is something that's always been really important to me.
嗯，你们知道这对我来说一直是非常重要的事情。

754
00:34:54.530 --> 00:35:00.610
And it was kind of the impetus and inspiration for starting Soul Pancake, a digital media company
这也是我创办数字媒体公司 Soul Pancake 的初衷和灵感来源，

755
00:35:00.610 --> 00:35:04.610
that, um, we, we, I created with some friends.
嗯，是我和一些朋友共同创立的。

756
00:35:04.610 --> 00:35:09.630
Um, but this whole idea of life's biggest possible questions has always really intrigued me.
关于人生终极问题的探讨，一直以来都让我非常着迷。

757
00:35:09.730 --> 00:35:15.990
You know, I took philosophy and in college and I love, you know, studying spirituality and
你知道，我在大学里修过哲学，我喜欢研究灵性，

758
00:35:15.990 --> 00:35:22.370
I love, you know, psychology and sociology and kind of creativity and how creativity works
我也喜欢心理学、社会学，还有创造力以及创造力是如何运作的，

759
00:35:22.370 --> 00:35:22.970
and why.
以及为什么会这样。

760
00:35:23.250 --> 00:35:28.610
And so this was kind of the, the foundation for metaphysical milkshake.
所以这算是《形而上奶昔》（Metaphysical Milkshake）的基石。

761
00:35:28.810 --> 00:35:33.650
Um, our first season we did on this company called Luminary, but that didn't really work
嗯，我们的第一季是在 Luminary 这个平台上做的，但效果不太理想，

762
00:35:33.650 --> 00:35:33.830
out.
没能成功。

763
00:35:33.930 --> 00:35:38.570
So now we're doing a second season, which is available wherever podcasts are, are available
所以现在我们正在做第二季，大家可以在任何播客平台上收听，

764
00:35:38.570 --> 00:35:41.350
and including a lot of the stuff we did for our first season.
其中也包含了我们第一季制作的很多内容。

765
00:35:41.830 --> 00:35:43.750
And, um, it's super fun.
而且，嗯，这真的超级有趣。

766
00:35:43.750 --> 00:35:48.130
We get to talk to just artists and thinkers and writers.
我们有机会与各种艺术家、思想家和作家交流。

767
00:35:48.690 --> 00:35:55.770
Um, we just yesterday interviewed Avi Loeb, who's the head of the, uh, uh, astronomy division
嗯，就在昨天，我们采访了哈佛大学天文学系主任 Avi Loeb，

768
00:35:55.770 --> 00:36:02.170
of Harvard university, talking about alien life, um, and discovering extraterrestrial life.
谈论了外星生命，以及如何发现地外生命。

769
00:36:02.350 --> 00:36:07.950
And, and then we had Jason, speaking of office auctions, Jason Isbell is one of my favorite
还有，说到办公室拍卖，Jason Isbell 是我最喜欢的，

770
00:36:07.950 --> 00:36:09.710
kind of country rock.
